Production-Level Concepts & Troubleshooting

For 2–4 years experience, interviewers expect you to design, operate, scale, and troubleshoot Kubernetes clusters, not just deploy a basic pod.

🔹 Kubernetes Interview Questions (2–4 yrs)

• What is Kubernetes and why is it used in production?
• Kubernetes architecture (Control Plane & Worker Nodes)
• Role of API Server, Scheduler, Controller Manager, etcd
• Pod vs Deployment vs StatefulSet vs DaemonSet
• ReplicaSet vs Deployment
• What happens when a pod crashes?
• Liveness vs Readiness vs Startup probes
• ConfigMap vs Secret
• How does Kubernetes handle service discovery?
• Service types (ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer)
• Ingress vs Service
• What is Helm and why is it used?
• Rolling updates and rollback in Kubernetes
• Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)
• How does Kubernetes handle node failure?
• Resource requests vs limits
• How do you secure Kubernetes workloads?
• RBAC in Kubernetes
• Namespaces and their importance
• Kubernetes networking basics (CNI)
• Pod-to-pod communication
• Node affinity vs pod affinity
• Taints and tolerations
• Stateful applications in Kubernetes
• Persistent Volumes (PV) & Persistent Volume Claims (PVC)
• Kubernetes secrets encryption
• Cluster upgrades strategy
• Multi-environment Kubernetes setup
• Kubernetes monitoring (Prometheus & Grafana)
• Pod stuck in CrashLoopBackOff — troubleshooting steps
• Application not accessible via Ingress — what will you check?
• Pods not scaling even when CPU is high — why?
• Node goes NotReady — what actions will you take?
• Deployment failed after update — how will you rollback?
• Config change without redeployment — how?
• Secrets accidentally exposed — mitigation steps

💡 Interview Tip:
If you say:
👉 “I troubleshoot using kubectl logs, describe, events, and metrics”
you already sound like a production-ready Kubernetes engineer.
